            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Birutė Galdikas - Early Life</strong><br>\nBirutė Galdikas was born on May 10, 1946, in Wiesbaden, Germany, to Lithuanian parents. Growing up, she became fascinated with wildlife and was particularly interested in primates. She moved to Canada with her family as a child and later attended the University of British Columbia, where she studied zoology and psychology. Galdikas' passion for animals led her to pursue graduate studies in anthropology at UCLA, setting the stage for her future research in primatology.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Academic Journey and Inspiration</strong><br>\nAt UCLA, Birutė Galdikas was inspired by the work of famed anthropologist Louis Leakey, who encouraged her interest in the great apes. She expressed a desire to study orangutans, which were the least understood of the great apes at the time. Her determination impressed Leakey, who helped secure funding for her research. Galdikas earned her Ph.D. with a focus on the behavior of orangutans in Borneo, marking her as one of Leakey's \"Trimates,\" a group dedicated to studying primates.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Orangutan Research in Borneo</strong><br>\nIn 1971, Galdikas began her fieldwork in Tanjung Puting National Park in Indonesian Borneo. She immersed herself in the study of wild orangutans, living in a remote rainforest camp. Her work shed light on many aspects of orangutan behavior, including their diet, social structure, and nesting habits. Galdikas faced numerous challenges, from difficult living conditions to resistance from the logging industry, but her research efforts persevered.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
