            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Conservation Efforts</strong><br>\nAlongside her research, Birutė Galdikas became deeply involved in conservation efforts for orangutans and their habitat. She founded the Orangutan Foundation International (OFI) in 1986, which works to protect orangutans and the rainforest. The foundation also rehabilitates orphaned or displaced orangutans and releases them back into the wild. Galdikas' advocacy has been crucial in bringing international attention to the threats facing these primates.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Educational Outreach</strong><br>\nGaldikas has made significant contributions to educating the public about orangutans and the environment. She has written books and articles and has been featured in documentaries to raise awareness about her work and the plight of the orangutans. Her outreach programs through OFI also involve local communities in Borneo, educating them on sustainable practices and the importance of conservation.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Awards and Recognition</strong><br>\nFor her extensive work, Birutė Galdikas has received numerous awards, including the Tyler Prize for Environmental Achievement and the Officer of the Order of Canada. She is recognized worldwide as a leading authority on orangutan behavior and conservation. Her tireless efforts have made her not just a scientist but also a global conservationist.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
