          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Influence on Primatology</strong><br>\nGaldikas' studies have greatly expanded the scientific community's knowledge of orangutans. Her research has influenced conservation policies and has played a pivotal role in primatology. Through her work, the scientific methods used to study primates in the wild have been refined, contributing to better understanding and protection strategies for these animals.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and Continuing Work</strong><br>\nBirutė Galdikas continues to be an active figure in primatology and conservation. Her legacy includes inspiring new generations of researchers and conservationists. She maintains her position as a professor and remains involved with OFI, overseeing its operations and ongoing research. Her work underscores the importance of long-term commitment to conservation.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Personal Life and Public Image</strong><br>\nGaldikas has balanced her demanding career with family life, often including her two children in her fieldwork. Her public image is that of a devoted scientist and conservationist, yet she also emphasizes the importance of family and community. Through her unique life story, Galdikas exemplifies how personal passion can lead to profound professional and global achievements.</p>\n"
              },
